# Explicit API Contracts

- Every API has explicit versioning from day one (`/v1/`, `/v2/`)
- Authentication and tenant identification are mandatory on every request
- Error responses follow a single structured pattern — never ad-hoc strings
- Pagination, sorting, and filtering follow a uniform convention
- Endpoints reflect the domain — not the database. Resources are named by business concepts

## Error Response Shape

Use a consistent envelope: error code, human-readable message, optional field-level details, correlation ID.

Resource names, DTOs, and OpenAPI descriptions must align with the domain glossary.
